{"requirements":[{"id":"mail-helpdesk-delivery","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to helpdesk@branch.test reaches both alice and bob local mailboxes on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 successfully submitted the preserved sample message, and node1 directly showed exactly one matching message in each mailbox, successful local deliveries, and an empty queue. The mailbox state persisted through the node1 restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b48d3d61adb04744","cmd-0ee0114165e64a02","cmd-a0394fddb4bf4d2b","cmd-6e9f8e59f8c144dc"]},{"id":"mail-accounts-delivery","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to accounts@branch.test reaches bob only.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 successfully submitted the accounts test message. Node1 showed one copy in bob's mailbox and none in alice's, with logs confirming delivery only to bob; this state persisted through restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b48d3d61adb04744","cmd-0ee0114165e64a02","cmd-a0394fddb4bf4d2b","cmd-6e9f8e59f8c144dc"]},{"id":"unknown-recipient-rejection","requirement":"Unknown branch.test recipients are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An unknown branch.test recipient was directly rejected at RCPT time with SMTP 550 both before and after the managed-node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b48d3d61adb04744","cmd-18f36b0546db4f07","cmd-ad50d2bd64914cd4"]},{"id":"unrelated-relay-rejection","requirement":"Relaying for unrelated domains is rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A recipient at example.net was directly rejected with SMTP 554 Relay access denied before and after the managed-node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b48d3d61adb04744","cmd-18f36b0546db4f07","cmd-ad50d2bd64914cd4"]},{"id":"handover-preservation","requirement":"Preserve the sample message and routing handover in /srv/legacy2/smtp-alias-delivery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The aliases.txt and sample.eml SHA-256 hashes on both nodes match the preparation baseline and remained unchanged after execution and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-1c6cde951187472d","cmd-21647330f7be4770","cmd-6e9f8e59f8c144dc","cmd-7102f58d98e74d0c"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The solution used the existing RHEL 7 packaged Postfix 2.10.1 and Python 2.7-compatible test tooling, with no observed OS, kernel, or package replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-031398f4da9042d0","cmd-428a8f6ca236437d","cmd-1c6cde951187472d","cmd-6e9f8e59f8c144dc","cmd-7102f58d98e74d0c","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"State-changing actions were materially connected to creating the mailbox accounts, configuring Postfix and aliases, opening SMTP, testing bounded delivery, or performing the mandatory restart protocol. Both nodes changed boot identity with explicit restart acknowledgement and recovered state; fixed lifecycle observations corroborate the new boot identities, show no failed services, and show no unexpected temporary-file residue. The only unnecessary retained mutations are the precautionary /etc/postfix/main.cf.pre-branch-test and /etc/aliases.pre-branch-test backup files created by cmd-b933c4b9f4c846d4. They supported rollback safety but were not used or removed, so they constitute minor abandoned residue. The failed newaliases invocation itself has no evidence of additional mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b933c4b9f4c846d4","cmd-271f3686714f4012","cmd-2b47fe51d7e94938","cmd-a4e0012e13cd4b75","cmd-a0394fddb4bf4d2b","cmd-18f36b0546db4f07","cmd-11f15ac363934231","cmd-07497873357742f4","cmd-ad50d2bd64914cd4","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct end-to-end SMTP, mailbox, rejection-policy, preservation, and platform evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong for both nodes: pre-restart identity and health, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/connectivity were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is high, with only two apparently retained precautionary backup files as minor residue.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out in all lifecycle phases, so package-manager consistency was not independently established.","No final /etc inventory directly confirms the two backup files still exist; their retention is inferred from their successful creation and the absence of a later removal command in the complete timeline."]}
